set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false
set_option warningAsError true
/-!
# The variational energy part of the local Stokes problem

The energy space is constructed as the closed subspace of `L²` generated by the
gradients of actual smooth compactly supported vector tests. Its divergence is
the continuous matrix trace map. Riesz representation on the closed divergence
kernel constructs the variational Stokes solution and proves its energy bound.
The residual factors through the actual divergence range, without assuming a
pressure projector or an inf-sup estimate.

Recovering a mean-zero `L²` pressure from this factorization additionally needs
a bounded right inverse for divergence on a ball. This module does not claim
that estimate or the pressure recovery theorem.
-/
@[expose] public section
open MeasureTheory Set CKN
open CKN.Foundation.Parabolic
open scoped ENNReal Topology BigOperators
set_option autoImplicit false
noncomputable section
namespace FluidSingularSets
/-- The Euclidean Hilbert norm on spatial gradient matrices. -/
abbrev StokesGradientMatrix := EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 3 × Fin 3)
end FluidSingularSets

end
end
end

-- ==== Examples.CoolRmal__FluidSingularSets.Examples.Example_a8964171df78c7cf4096_StokesNonlinearPressure ====
